---
description: Survey-math and contract rules for Deed Reader Pro
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md, docs/CONTRACTS.md, and docs/RECONCILE.md before writing code. Also follow .cursor/rules/deedreadrule.mdc.

- The app is deed-reader-web/frontend (npm, React, CRA) and deed-reader-web/backend (Flask on port 5000, FastAPI migration in progress). Do not add pnpm, Next.js, Prisma, or packages/.
- New survey math lives only in deed-reader-web/backend/core and is deterministic. Do not use an AI number as geometry. The existing bearing_decimal path in services/plotting_service.py stays until docs/REQUESTS.md says to replace it.
- Do not edit docs/CONTRACTS.md unless the task is 00-foundation or 06-contracts-update. Do not rename existing fields. Put change requests in docs/REQUESTS.md.
- Work only inside the paths the assigned task owns.
- Never overwrite user edits; create a new DeedVersion once editing exists.
- Do not import anthropic or openai outside services/claude_service.py. Keys come from the environment.
- New persisted queries take a firm id once accounts exist. Existing routes are not firm-scoped.
- Run python lint.py, npm run lint, and npx tsc --noEmit before opening a pull request. New behavior needs a pytest or Jest assertion.
